    "formation_name": "Cruiser Wall, Torpedo Reserve",
    "selection_rationale": "Uniform 1.5g strike group: one cruiser_torpedo provides a 48-round saturation salvo (enough volume to overwhelm PD and crack a capital's armor), escorted by three gun cruisers (spinal coilers + coilgun batteries + heavy armor + PD) that screen the torpedo boat during approach and finish crippled targets. A cheap frigate adds extra PD dwell and coilgun fire for minimal cost. All hulls share speed so the formation stays coherent instead of fragmenting into a fast/slow split.",
    "formation_rationale": "The three Bastion cruisers form a forward line with modest lateral spread (~45 km apart) so they overlap point-defense coverage while presenting a wider target picture to complicate the enemy's spinal weapon geometry. They absorb the initial exchange and screen the vulnerable torpedo cruiser. Harpoon (our torpedo boat) is held far back at -70 km to stay out of early gun range and preserve it for a decisive torpedo salvo once ranges close or enemy PD is suppressed. Ward, the small frigate, sits just behind the cruiser line and ahead of Harpoon, adding close-in PD support for the torpedo cruiser without exposing its low HP to the front line.",
